  "caveats": [
    "This is a standalone kernel diagnostic, not a model throughput comparison or a physical bus measurement.",
    "n_keep=null, t_out_begin=0: state is read-only as in verification; commit/replay kernels are not measured.",
    "Current model defaults to SIMD16; SIMD32 is an explicit spilling-kernel control, not a proposed default.",
    "Explicit dependency barrier after each launch on relaxed lists; two GPU timestamps add fixed overhead.",
    "GPU timestamps use previously calibrated Windows 19.2MHz/36-bit CS domain, not rounded public nanoseconds.",
    "Two overwritten fixture phases, each 200ms conditioning plus10warmups+30retained; unlocked clocks.",
    "Allocation implementations differ; host/local requested placement is not continuously observed.",
    "Setup/copies/reference/full-guard validation and initialization are outside timed replay. No Linux GPU run.",
    "Each summary is the median of two fixture-phase medians, not a pooled median.",
    "The 16-launch chain reuses one state/input region; it does not reproduce the model working set or mixed-kernel transitions.",
    "GPU-time differences are separate from submit-and-wait wall time; neither establishes an end-to-end native win.",
    "Output dumps concatenate FP32 y and packed Q8 tails; both phases match byte-for-byte across all six arms.",
    "Input/state/prefix/tail/padding guards and timestamp guards are checked in the executable; scalar reference covers FP32 y.",
    "Packed Q8 outputs additionally pass finite-scale/quantization checks and cross-backend byte parity, not an independent CPU quantization oracle."
  ],
